        guidedApproach = "Divide by 2 → centre & radius → find slope → negative reciprocal through centre.",
        guidedSolution = "x²+y²−4x+6y−3=0 → Centre (2, −3), Radius r = √(4+9+3) = 4. Perpendicular slope = +2/3 → y − (−3) = (2/3)(x − 2) → 3y + 9 = 2x − 4 → 2x − 3y = 13.",
        projTitle = "Estate Street Intersection Perpendicularity Audit",
        projScenario = "Road 1 passes through A(1, 2) and B(5, 4); Road 2 passes through C(3, 6) and D(5, 2). Prove geometrically whether they meet at 90° and find the intersection coordinates.",
